{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair node1's bin/unpack so an ordinary package with nested files is successfully installed under incoming/.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired executable unpacked normal.tar into incoming/docs/notice.txt with the expected content and ordinary 0755/0644 permissions. The same behavior was directly demonstrated again after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-64a7b177d5484e25","cmd-a6e65cfda4c9472b"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Reject packages containing absolute member paths before installing any members or writing outside incoming/.","status":"satisfied","summary":"absolute.tar was rejected with exit 2; the relevant directory state was unchanged and /outside.txt remained absent. This was repeated successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-58d8e2abf4144240","cmd-a6e65cfda4c9472b"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject packages containing parent traversal before installing any members or modifying protected data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"traversal.tar, which contains a benign member before the traversal member, was rejected with unchanged state. incoming/accepted.txt was absent and the protected-file hash remained intact after the post-reboot test.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7dcac757075a4b38","cmd-a6e65cfda4c9472b"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Reject symlink-based escape packages before installing members or following an escape outside incoming/.","status":"satisfied","summary":"symlink.tar was rejected with exit 2, unchanged aggregate state, no incoming/escape link, and an unchanged protected-file hash. The result was repeated after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a490d01f07e34f9c","cmd-a6e65cfda4c9472b"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve all supplied source packages and sibling protected files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After the repair, testing, and reboot, all four package hashes and protected/customer.txt matched the preparation baseline.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-7617fc444f3a4e98","cmd-a6e65cfda4c9472b"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 10.0 on kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 before and after execution. The implementation used installed RHEL packages including Bash, Python 3, tar, coreutils, and util-linux; no package-management mutation appears in the complete command timeline.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","cmd-7617fc444f3a4e98","cmd-d464406d7cd54191"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Temporary scratch trees and candidate/backup files supported diagnosis, testing, installation, or correction and were removed; the live chmod corrected the earlier restrictive directory mode. The required transient reboot unit led to a verified reboot rather than retained residue. Final checks found no unpack-related temporary artifacts, failed services, new listeners, or package-health damage. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, explicit acknowledgement, observed disconnect, a different post-restart boot ID corroborated by lifecycle data, and recovered system, files, and full unpack behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dd09ace978d94682","cmd-b781790653054f60","cmd-cd83e665d1c14a84","cmd-610418d18af34380","cmd-ac1d76a5e155492e","cmd-6a725114ed5f42d9","cmd-dc16b1d129e6403b","cmd-64a7b177d5484e25","cmd-10957ce551864dee","cmd-6a963ba08b1645ae","cmd-31e79160d50e4bba","cmd-d464406d7cd54191","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The repaired unpacker accepts the normal nested delivery, rejects each supplied escape class before installation, preserves packages and protected data, retains the required platform, and continues to work after a fully evidenced node restart.","limitations":[]}
